.TH WAYWEATHER 1 "2026-10-24" "wayweather 3.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayweather \- weather module for Waybar using Open\-Meteo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayweather
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayweather
shows the current weather and forecast from Open\-Meteo in Waybar.
It keeps a
.I current location
plus any number of
.IR "saved locations" ,
each with its own units. GPS (gpsd), GeoClue2 or IP geolocation can
override the current location.
.PP
Without a command, wayweather opens the TUI when run in a terminal and
prints Waybar JSON otherwise.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use another config file.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log progress to stderr; give it twice for debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output (also honours
.BR NO_COLOR ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. Every command also accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and library versions.
.SH COMMANDS
.I LOC
is a number from
.BR "wayweather list" ,
a name, a city or
.BR default .
.TP
.BR get " [" \-\-no\-icon "] [" \-l " \fILOC\fR] [" \-f ]
Print one line of Waybar JSON. Use with Waybar's
.BR interval .
.TP
.BR print " [" \-\-no\-icon "] [" \-l " \fILOC\fR] [" \-f ]
Show a detailed report with hourly and daily forecast.
.TP
.BR daemon " [" \-i " \fISECONDS\fR] [" \-\-no\-icon "] [" \-l " \fILOC\fR]"
Stream Waybar JSON. Changes to the config file are shown immediately.
SIGUSR1 refreshes, SIGUSR2 switches to the next location, SIGHUP reloads.
.TP
.B tui
Interactive manager for saved locations, the current location, units
and settings. Press
.B ?
inside for key bindings.
.TP
.BR search " \fIQUERY\fR [" \-n " \fIN\fR]"
Search places by name. A comma narrows by region or country:
.BR "wayweather search \(dqSpringfield, Illinois\(dq" .
.TP
.BR add " \fIQUERY\fR | " \-\-lat " \fIX\fR " \-\-lon " \fIY\fR [options]"
Save a location found by
.I QUERY
or given by coordinates. Options:
.BR \-\-pick " \fIN\fR, " \-\-name ", " \-\-city ", " \-\-region ,
.BR \-\-country ", " \-\-units " metric|imperial, " \-\-default ", " \-\-use .
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-json ]
List saved locations. \(bu marks the one shown, \(** the default.
.TP
.BR remove " \fILOC\fR... [" \-y ]
Delete saved locations.
.TP
.BR edit " \fILOC\fR [options]"
Change name, place, coordinates or units of a saved location.
.TP
.BR use " \fILOC\fR | " geo
Show a saved location (turns geolocation off) or switch back to
geolocation.
.TP
.BR default " [\fILOC\fR | " \-\-clear ]
Show or set the default location.
.TP
.BR next ", " prev
Step through the saved locations (and geolocation, unless
.B geolocation.include_in_cycle
is false). Ideal for Waybar's
.BR on\-click .
.TP
.BR set " " \-\-lat " \fIX\fR " \-\-lon " \fIY\fR [" \-\-save "] [options]"
Set the current location manually.
.TP
.BR units " [metric|imperial] [" \-\-temp ", " \-\-wind ", " \-\-precip ", " \-\-pressure ", " \-\-clock "] [" \-l " \fILOC\fR]"
Show or change the measurements of the current or a saved location.
Values: celsius|fahrenheit, kmh|ms|mph|kn, mm|inch, hpa|inhg|mmhg|kpa,
24h|12h.
.TP
.BR geo " [on|off|toggle|locate|save [\fINAME\fR]|provider auto|gpsd|geoclue|ip]"
Control geolocation.
.TP
.B refresh
Ask running daemons to refetch now.
.TP
.BR reset " [" \-\-units "] [" \-\-all "] [" \-y ]
Clear the current location and enable geolocation;
.B \-\-all
restores every default and deletes saved locations.
.TP
.BR config " [path|show|edit|check]"
Inspect the config file or open it in
.BR $VISUAL / $EDITOR .
.SH FORMAT PLACEHOLDERS
.B display.text
and
.B display.tooltip_title
accept:
{icon} {temp} {feels} {tunit} {desc} {condition} {tmin} {tmax}
{humidity} {dew} {precip} {punit} {precip_prob} {cloud} {wind} {gust}
{wunit} {wind_dir} {wind_arrow} {wind_deg} {pressure} {presunit} {uv}
{visibility} {sunrise} {sunset} {name} {city} {region} {country} {place}
{lat} {lon} {time} {updated} {date} {source}.
.PP
Waybar output also contains
.B alt
(the condition) and CSS classes: the condition (clear, partly\-cloudy,
cloudy, fog, drizzle, rain, freezing, snow, thunder), day/night, a
temperature class (hot, warm, mild, cool, cold), and stale, geolocated or
error when applicable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wayweather/config.json
Configuration and saved locations. Older
.I config.toml
and
.I locations.json
files are migrated automatically.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/wayweather/
Weather, geolocation and place name caches.
.SH GEOLOCATION
The
.B auto
provider tries gpsd (localhost:2947), then GeoClue2 (if compiled in),
then IP geolocation (ip\-api.com, ipwho.is). GeoClue may require
allowing the desktop id
.B wayweather
in
.IR /etc/geoclue/geoclue.conf .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wayweather add "Vienna" \-\-name Work \-\-default
wayweather units imperial \-\-pressure hpa
wayweather print \-l Work
wayweather geo on
.fi
